/* ── block 40 · index.html:28440 ── */

          /* Fleet Bridge chrome · brought to the TCP spec so the
             header strip + cmd-tabs match Schedule + Onboarding
             pixel-for-pixel. Tokens live in dashboard/tcp.css:
               --tcp-strip-h     = 115px
               --tcp-cmd-tabs-h  =  28px
               --tcp-title-w     = 240px
             Per operator preference there's no KPI strip on this
             surface — Fleet Bridge stops at the header card and
             the email grid takes over. */
          /* cmd-shell · flex-column wrapper. cmd-tabs sit IN-FLOW
             above the strip card (same pattern as Onboarding); the
             previous absolute positioning made the strip card sit
             ~28px higher than Schedule's because the tabs ate no
             in-flow space. With the tabs in-flow the strip card
             lands at the same Y as Schedule's. */
          #view-email .em-cmd-shell{
