/* ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   Header clean pass (operator request 2026-06-11)
   --------------------------------------------------------------------
   1. The Ask-AI pill is removed from the topbar. The form element stays
      in the DOM (display:none) because the Ctrl+K command palette's
      "Ask RouteReady: …" fallback row submits through
      #rr-hdr-ask-input / #rr-hdr-ask-form — hiding (not deleting)
      keeps that path alive. Ctrl+K remains the way to ask.
   2. The cmd-tab bands (SCHEDULE / WORKFLOWS / PRINT-DOWNLOAD and the
      per-view mirrors) are removed on every TCP view so all strips
      stay in lockstep. The tab BUTTONS also stay in the DOM — the
      palette's "Workflows strip" / "Print / Download" commands drive
      the same delegated .sched-cmd-tab click path.
   3. The freed band height (--tcp-cmd-tabs-h → 0 in tcp.css) pulls
      every command icon strip up the page.
   ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
.topbar .hdr-ask{display:none!important}
/* The Ask pill was the topbar's flex spacer (flex:1; margin:0 auto).
   With it hidden, right-align the bar and let the QAT (the left
   cluster) push everything after it to the right edge. Works whether
   or not individual right-side tools are visible (theme toggle /
   refresh render conditionally). */
.topbar{justify-content:flex-end}
.topbar .rr-qat{margin-right:auto}
/* Per-view ID selectors included: schedule-rrx.css pins the schedule band
   with `#view-schedule.rrx-schedule .sched-v2-cmd-tabs{display:inline-flex
   !important}` (and other views may pin theirs the same way), so the hide
   rules must match or beat that specificity. */
#view-schedule.rrx-schedule .sched-v2-cmd-tabs.sched-cmd-tabs,
.sched-v2-cmd-tabs,.f2-cmd-tabs,.ob-cmd-tabs,.em-cmd-tabs,.wf-cmd-tabs,.ws-cmd-tabs,
